Subject: [PATCH] avcodec: keep CREATE_BUFS failures negative

create_dst_bufs() saves -errno, but negates it a second time when returning.
Its caller treats that positive value as an allocated buffer count. A
failed allocation can therefore publish uncreated qents and walk beyond
the requested qent array, instead of returning an allocation failure.

Return the saved negative error so the existing failure path releases the
uncreated qents without indexing or publishing them. Compare it with
-EINTR so interrupted calls actually retry. Preserve partial-success
handling; do not change pool size or codec DPB demand.

--- a/libavcodec/v4l2_req_media.c
+++ b/libavcodec/v4l2_req_media.c
@@ -1160,7 +1160,7 @@ static int create_dst_bufs(struct mediabufs_ctl *const mbc, unsigned int n, struct qent_dst * const qes[])
         const int err = -errno;
-        if (err != EINTR) {
+        if (err != -EINTR) {
             request_err(mbc->dc, "%s: Failed to create V4L2 buffer\n", __func__);
-            return -err;
+            return err;
         }
     }
 
